    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **21 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization for owner creation. The normalization rule \u2014 trim, collapse internal whitespace to a single space, upper-case, then expand the whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE` \u2014 lives in one shared, idempotent helper so the stored/returned value and every comparison use an identical canonical form.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`OwnerAddresses.java`** (new) \u2014 the shared `normalize(String)` utility, mirroring the existing `OwnerEmails` helper. `null`/all-whitespace normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n- **`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 normalizes the address in place *before* the required-field check. Because `ValidateOwnerFields` is the first step (the only one that binds `@RequestBody`) and publishes the body for later steps, this is the correct place to normalize: it makes the required check reject an address that is blank after normalization, and the normalized value then flows through `BuildOwner` to what's stored and returned.\n\n- **`EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`** \u2014 both the household duplicate-detection comparison and the shared `householdId` derivation now compare `OwnerAddresses.normalize(...)` on each side (request and every existing owner), so seed data or any pre-existing record is compared on the normalized form too. The `lastName` canonicalization is unchanged.\n\n**How the new tests are satisfied:**\n- Cp12: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`; `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`; `\"   \"` \u2192 400.\n- Cp01: whitespace-only address rejected (blank after normalization); missing city still rejected.\n- Cp10: `\"12 Main St\"` and `\"12  main  street\"` both normalize to `\"12 MAIN STREET\"` \u2192 409 duplicate.\n- Cp11: `\"12 main street\"` and `\"12  MAIN  ST\"` normalize equal \u2192 same derived `householdId`.\n\nThe `PUT` (update) pipeline's `ApplyOwner` was intentionally left untouched, since the change is scoped to owner creation.",
